\tr{\td{P1 gates}\td{measurement campaigns: threads, order, session cap, platform, \code{\verb~|-march~}; proposals for defaults}\td{M4}\td{A6.8, A7.1}\td{the four decision tables of this document filled with mathlib numbers}}
\tr{\td{H1 hardening}\td{fuzzing of reader + loader (grammar-based and mutational), resource-exhaustion behaviour, determinism soak}\td{L1, D2}\td{A3.4, A8}\td{no status other than 1, 2 (or 3 for an injected \code{\verb~|Error~}) on 10^6 fuzzed inputs; never 0 on a mutant the official checker rejects}}
}

\p{The machine's own packages are in \code{\verb~|ISA.md~}; its integration point is one class (\code{\verb~|EngineProvider~} named "machine") and the differential harness of T1.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{11. Boundary to ISA.md}

\p{Provided to the machine:}

\ul{
\li{the store API of section 1.3 with the layouts of section 2 (normative: \code{\verb~|rlvm.store.Node~}), including per-node \code{\verb~|fvMask~} that never under-approximates, \code{\verb~|looseRange~}, \code{\verb~|HAS_LPARAM~}, \code{\verb~|depMax~}, \code{\verb~|lpSet~}, and three header bits plus the \code{\verb~|c~} word of LAM/PI nodes for the elaborator's own static facts;}
\li{constant rows and derived inductive facts readable for every unit below \code{\verb~|envUnits~}; \code{\verb~|Specials~} with guard states (\code{\verb~|natOk~}, \code{\verb~|boolOk~}, \code{\verb~|stringOk~} of ISA.md 2.9 are \code{\verb~|state(NAT..)~}, \code{\verb~|state(BOOL..)~}, \code{\verb~|state(STRING..)~}); \code{\verb~|SharedFacts~} as the shared check-mode table (\code{\verb~|PCHK~});}
\li{a \code{\verb~|WorkerContext~} per session: term overlay (decodes proof blocks, holds terms the machine builds), list / level / literal overlays, \code{\verb~|RunSignals~} (first failure, memory);}
\li{lifecycle: sessions only move forward in rank; \code{\verb~|reset()~} is called by the driver on the conditions of 6.4 and always before a cold or strict run; \code{\verb~|Terms.refresh()~} at every unit start;}
\li{preconditions of \code{\verb~|Session.check~} (4.3) and the guarantee that a REJECT is confirmed elsewhere.}
}

\p{Required from the machine:}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|Engine~} / \code{\verb~|Session~} as specified in \code{\verb~|rlvm.api~}, registered as an \code{\verb~|EngineProvider~};}
\li{outcomes that are functions of ids (I3), nothing kept from abandoned or failed work, DECLINE on every limit, termination on ill-typed input (I4);}
\li{no writes to shared store data other than \code{\verb~|SharedFacts~} and its own engine-wide tables, which must be safe under concurrent sessions and must not make a verdict depend on which session filled them;}
\li{\code{\verb~|EngineConfig.strict~} (no shortcut, no cache across units) for the re-check, \code{\verb~|footprintBytes()~} and \code{\verb~|steps()~} that are cheap and honest, \code{\verb~|dumpStats~} for heat;}
\li{\code{\verb~|KernelOps~} from the machine is optional; admission uses the reference kernel in v1.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{12. Risks and open questions}

\p{Risks:}

\ol{
\li{\strong{AOT code quality} (7.1): if the gate is not run, up to 1.4x of the machine's instructions is left on the table; if it picks the JVM, start-up and warm-up variance (about 2 \%) enters every measurement.}
\li{\strong{Exact syntactic regeneration of recursors} (R03 6.13) is the largest correctness item outside the machine; a mismatch rejects a good file. Mitigation: Init's 605 and mathlib's 7,129 blocks as regression corpus from M2 on.}
\li{\strong{Reference kernel speed} decides whether rejections are confirmed within timeouts and whether the fallback rescues mathlib; its floor is set by acceptance criteria (R3), not by hope.}
\li{\strong{Pipelined loading} depends on a level-store snapshot; without it the wall-clock model of 3.5 loses 15 s on mathlib (batch mode), nothing else.}
\li{\strong{Shared-region estimate} (36 \% of records) comes from Susz's numbers for an earlier mathlib; a growth copy costs a transient 1.8 GB. Mitigation: measured ratio at M3, head-room adjusted.}
\li{\strong{Optimistic environment} makes every engine face ill-typed bodies; a hang there is contained by budgets and cancellation only if polls are frequent (ISA.md 1.4).}
\li{\strong{Parallel overhead} above 2 \% would cost rank; the gate then lowers the default, at the price of wall clock.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|Error~} handling}: a \code{\verb~|StackOverflowError~} in the reference kernel ends the run with status 3 under the launcher's contract; depth accounting must be conservative.}
}

\p{Open questions:}

\ul{
\li{O1. Does the level store get \code{\verb~|snapshot()~} (1.4)? Otherwise pipelining needs its own level table in \code{\verb~|rlvm-load~}.}
\li{O2. May the arena build download Oracle GraalVM (GFTC) if PGO wins the platform gate?}
\li{O3. AoS (this document) or columns (R11 B.3, ISA.md 1.1 wording) for term nodes: decided by WP-A1's measurement in the image; the accessor API is the same.}
\li{O4. String-literal hook for exports of Lean < 4.36 (\code{\verb~|String.mk~} against \code{\verb~|String.ofList~}): do navier-stokes-euler and reachability (4.34.x) contain string literals that must expand? (R01 6.5)}
\li{O5. Forward references and generated-but-unlisted constants: decline in v1; implement only if an arena test appears.}
\li{O6. Session cap, order policy, worker count, scan helpers: defaults above are starting values; the gates of 6.2, 6.4, 6.8 decide.}
\li{O7. Is the arena's instruction count user-only (R01 1.2)? If kernel instructions count, page faults of the 4 GB working set and \code{\verb~|read~} copies become costs; \code{\verb~|MAP_POPULATE~}-style pre-touching would then be wrong and array reuse more valuable.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{Appendix A. Parent pom and build notes for the orchestrator}

\p{Lines to add to \code{\verb~|<modules>~} of the parent \code{\verb~|pom.xml~} (Maven orders the reactor by dependencies, so the position among the existing entries does not matter):}

\pre{\verb~|
    <module>rlvm-store</module>
    <module>rlvm-api</module>
    <module>rlvm-load</module>
    <module>rlvm-ref</module>
    <module>rlvm-inductive</module>
    <module>rlvm-admit</module>
    <module>rlvm-driver</module>
    <module>rlvm-main</module>
    <module>rlvm-testkit</module>
~}

\ul{
\li{The nine modules were compiled together through a temporary aggregator pom outside the tree (\code{\verb~|mvn -o -q -f <aggregator>/pom.xml compile~}: exit 0, 9 modules, 73 source files); \code{\verb~|rlvm-store~} also compiles alone with \code{\verb~|-f rlvm-store/pom.xml~}.}
\li{Modules with RLVM dependencies cannot be built alone with \code{\verb~|-pl MODULE~} unless the upstream jars are in \code{\verb~|.toolchain/m2~} (\code{\verb~|scripts/dev.sh install MODULE~}) or \code{\verb~|-am~} is given.}
\li{Dependencies to add when the wave-2a APIs are frozen: \code{\verb~|rlvm-api~} -> \code{\verb~|rlvm-level~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-nat~} (bindings); \code{\verb~|rlvm-load~} -> \code{\verb~|rlvm-export~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-level~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-nat~}; \code{\verb~|rlvm-main~} -> \code{\verb~|rlvm-cli~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-export~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-level~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-nat~}. \code{\verb~|rlvm-ref~} ships \code{\verb~|META-INF/services/rlvm.api.EngineProvider~}; \code{\verb~|rlvm-main~} will ship \code{\verb~|META-INF/services/rlvm.cli.Checker~}.}
\li{Names reserved for the machine: modules \code{\verb~|rlvm-machine~} (\code{\verb~|rlvm.machine~}) and \code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~} (\code{\verb~|rlvm.truffle~}).}
}
}
